Description: Standalone R implementation of TerraLink 1.7 habitat
    connectivity corridor optimization for raster and vector workflows.
    Supports scenario-based corridor planning with budget-constrained
    optimization, optional impassable areas, packaged parity fixtures,
    and comparative PRE/POST connectivity metrics. The package exposes
    TerraLink's structural, movement-oriented, and species-oriented
    strategy set in a scriptable R workflow that stays aligned with the
    QGIS plugin while avoiding a desktop GIS dependency. Methods and
    interpretation are informed by Gustafson (1998)
    <https://research.fs.usda.gov/treesearch/12046> and Kupfer (2012)
    <doi:10.1177/0309133312439594>.
